{
  "an6.57:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.57 ",
  "an6.57:0.2": "6. The Great Chapter ",
  "an6.57:0.3": "The Six Classes of Rebirth ",
  "an6.57:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. ",
  "an6.57:1.2": "Then Venerable Ānanda went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an6.57:1.3": "“Sir, Pūraṇa Kassapa describes six classes of rebirth: ",
  "an6.57:1.4": "black, blue, red, yellow, white, and ultimate white. ",
  "an6.57:2.1": "The black class of rebirth consists of slaughterers of sheep, pigs, poultry, or deer, hunters or fishers, bandits, executioners, butchers of cattle, jailers, and any others with a cruel livelihood. ",
  "an6.57:3.1": "The blue class of rebirth consists of mendicants whose life is thorny, and any others who teach the efficacy of deeds and action. ",
  "an6.57:4.1": "The red class of rebirth consists of the Jain ascetics who wear one cloth. ",
  "an6.57:5.1": "The yellow class of rebirth consists of the lay people dressed in white who are disciples of the naked ascetics. ",
  "an6.57:6.1": "The white class of rebirth consists of male and female Ājīvaka ascetics. ",
  "an6.57:7.1": "And the ultimate white class of rebirth consists of Nanda Vaccha, Kisa Saṅkicca, and the bamboo-staffed ascetic Gosāla. ",
  "an6.57:8.1": "These are the six classes of rebirth that Pūraṇa Kassapa describes.” ",
  "an6.57:9.1": "“But Ānanda, did the whole world authorize Pūraṇa Kassapa to describe these six 